#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""caffe: keep the Mac awake, with a café table of your running agent sessions.

Every interactive Copilot CLI / Codex CLI / Claude Code / Pi / OpenCode session
gets a card: a cup of coffee, its project, and what it's doing. Brewing coffee
steams and swirls as it's stirred; a session that finished its turn is ready, with
a biscuit on the saucer; one left alone goes cold. Ready orders come first.
When a session ends, its cup drains and the barista cat knocks it off the
table. The cat also sniffs new orders, chases the odd mouse, and naps when the
bar is quiet. Stray cats drop by now and then, and at 14:30 there's fika.

On battery at 20% or less, the display may sleep; agents keep running.

Each open app gets a latte, with its CPU and RAM. Running local Copilot app
sessions and chats also get cards labelled "Agent"; idle ones are hidden. T3 Code
sessions get cards that say exactly what they're doing.

The pictures need a terminal with the kitty graphics protocol, such as Ghostty,
kitty, WezTerm or a recent iTerm2. Other terminals get the cards without pictures.
Press p to pet the cat, f to feed it a treat, and q (or Ctrl-C) to close the bar
and get your receipt.

`caffe update` installs upstream over this copy, replacing local customizations.
"""

